<clickhouse>
    <!--
      The server-level memory tracker in this containerised setup over-counts badly: it
      reports 5.40 GiB committed while process RSS sits at 1.15 GiB, and a restart clears
      it. Queries were then killed non-deterministically by the OvercommitTracker while
      the container had gigabytes free.

      Real safety comes from the PER-QUERY ceiling the refresh job sets
      (max_memory_usage=3 GB with spill-to-disk below that), which bounds what any single
      query can actually use. This ratio gives the over-counting server tracker enough
      headroom that it stops arbitrating.
    -->
    <max_server_memory_usage_to_ram_ratio>4</max_server_memory_usage_to_ram_ratio>
</clickhouse>
